-A unit vector is simply a vector whose magnitude is equal to 1.  Given any
-vector :math:`\mathbf{v}` we can define a unit vector as:
-
-.. math::
-  \mathbf{\hat{n}_v} = \frac{\mathbf{v}}{\Vert \mathbf{v} \Vert}
