-    The G function is defined as the following integral:
-
-    .. math ::
-         \frac{1}{2 \pi i} \int_L \frac{\prod_{j=1}^m \Gamma(b_j - s)
-         \prod_{j=1}^n \Gamma(1 - a_j + s)}{\prod_{j=m+1}^q \Gamma(1- b_j +s)
